# Difference Between Memory Bus and Wishbone

The previous project used a simplified custom bus.

For example:

Custom Memory Bus

Address
Data
Read
Write
Ready

Wishbone provides a defined interface:

Wishbone

ADR
DAT
CYC
STB
WE
ACK

The important difference is that Wishbone defines a common protocol for how these signals are used.

This means that independently designed hardware components can use the same interface to communicate.

---

# Why Wishbone Matters for an SoC

A real SoC can contain many different components.

For example:

                    CPU
                     │
                     ▼
              ┌─────────────┐
              │   Wishbone  │
              │     Bus     │
              └──────┬──────┘
                     │
          ┌──────────┼──────────┐
          ▼          ▼          ▼
        RAM         UART       GPIO

Each peripheral can implement a Wishbone interface.

This allows the CPU to communicate with many different components using the same basic bus architecture.

This is one of the concepts needed to understand a complete SoC.

